{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Note that the beam number does not distinguish sets of beams that overlap, as it does for slur and other"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elements. Beaming groups are distinguished by being in different voices and\/or the presence or absence of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"grace and cue elements."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Beams that have a begin value can also have a fan attribute to indicate accelerandos and ritardandos using"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fanned beams. The fan attribute may also be used with a continue value if the fanning direction changes on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that note. The value is “none” if not specified."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The repeater attribute has been deprecated in MusicXML 3.0. Formerly used for tremolos, it needs to be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"specified with a “yes” value for each beam using it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps the MusicXML "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<beam>"},{"type":"text","text":" element."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Beam values include begin, continue, end, forward hook, and backward hook. Up to eight concurrent beams are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"available to cover up to 1024th notes. Each beam in a note is represented with a separate beam element,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"starting with the eighth note beam using a number attribute of 1."}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/s8CopyableP":{"title":"Swift.Copyable","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8CopyableP","type":"unresolvable"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLBeam":{"role":"symbol","url":"